The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
tile->mem.kernel_bb_pool = xe_sa_bo_manager_init(tile, SZ_1M, 16);
if (IS_ERR(tile->mem.kernel_bb_pool))
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because if the initialization of `kernel_bb_pool` fails (i.e., it returns an error), the function continues to execute, leading to the execution of subsequent operations like applying workarounds and initializing sysfs, which should not happen if the initialization has already failed.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (IS_ERR(tile->mem.kernel_bb_pool)) {
    err = PTR_ERR(tile->mem.kernel_bb_pool);
    goto err_mem_access;
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a proper error handling mechanism that immediately jumps to the error handling section if the initialization of `kernel_bb_pool` fails. This prevents unnecessary operations from being executed when the initialization has already failed, thus avoiding further errors or undefined behavior in the driver.

